        "content": "# Module 4: Basic Kubernetes Objects & Pods\n\n---\n\n## 4.1 Introduction to Pods\n\n# 4.1 Introduction to Pods\n\n#\n\n## 4.1 Introduction to Pods\nA **Pod** is the smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes.\n\n> **In simple words:**\n> A Pod is a wrapper that contains one or more containers.\n---\n### Real-Time Example 📦\nImagine ordering food online.\n- The food is placed inside a **delivery box**.\n- The delivery person carries the **box**, not raw food directly.\n**Analogy:**\n- Container = Food\n- Pod = Delivery Box\n- Kubernetes = Delivery Person\n---\n### Pod Components & Shared Resources\nContainers inside the same Pod share:\n- **Shared Network**: Same IP address and port space (communicate via `localhost`).\n- **Shared Storage**: Mounted Volumes to exchange files.\n\n---\n\n## 4.2 Writing Pod & Deployment YAML Manifests\n\n# 4.2 Writing Pod & Deployment YAML Manifests\n\n#\n\n## 4.2 Writing Pod & Deployment YAML Manifests\nKubernetes recommends defining objects declaratively using **YAML files**.\n\n### Sample Pod YAML (`pod.yaml`)\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: nginx-pod\n  labels:\n    app: web\nspec:\n  containers:\n  - name: nginx-container\n    image: nginx:latest\n    ports:\n    - containerPort: 80\n```\n---\n### Applying & Managing YAML Files\n```bash\n# Apply YAML configuration\nkubectl apply -f pod.yaml\n\n# View Pod details\nkubectl describe pod nginx-pod\n\n# View Pod logs\nkubectl logs nginx-pod\n\n# Delete Pod\nkubectl delete -f pod.yaml\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4.3 Environment Variables\n\n# 4.3 Environment Variables\n\n## Env Variables\nInject configurations into container environments from ConfigMaps/Secrets.\n\n---\n\n## 4.4 Kubernetes Volumes\n\n# 4.4 Kubernetes Volumes\n\n## Volumes\nMount host paths or ephemeral emptyDirs directly to container runtimes.\n\n---\n\n## 4.5 PersistentVolumes & PVC\n\n# 4.5 PersistentVolumes & PVC\n\n## PV & PVC\nProvision persistent storage resources and bind them to container claims.\n\n---\n\n## 4.6 StorageClasses\n\n# 4.6 StorageClasses\n\n## StorageClasses\nConfigure dynamic provisioning parameters to allocate cloud storage.\n\n---\n\n## 4.7 Resource Requests & Limits\n\n# 4.7 Resource Requests & Limits\n\n## Resource Limits\nPrevent container resource leaks by setting CPU/Memory requests and bounds.\n\n---\n\n## 4.8 Practice: Deploy App with Storage\n\n# 4.8 Practice: Deploy App with Storage\n\n## ⚠️ Practice Only\nDeploy stateful web apps with PVC.",
