        "content": "# Module 5: Services & Networking\n\n---\n\n## 5.1 What is a Kubernetes Service?\n\n# 5.1 What is a Kubernetes Service?\n\n#\n\n## 5.1 What is a Kubernetes Service?\nA **Service** is an abstraction object that defines a logical set of Pods and a policy by which to access them (stable IP address & DNS entry).\n\n---\n### Why Do We Need Services?\nPods are **ephemeral** (temporary). When a Pod crashes and restarts:\n- A new Pod gets a **new IP address**.\n- Without a Service, clients using the old IP address will fail!\nA **Service** provides a permanent IP address and load balances traffic automatically across matching Pods.\n\n---\n### 4 Types of Kubernetes Services 1. **ClusterIP** *(Default)*: Accessible only inside the cluster (e.g. Backend microservices, databases).\n2. **NodePort**: Exposes the service on each Node's IP at a static port (30000-32767). 3. **LoadBalancer**: Provisions an external Cloud Load Balancer (AWS ELB, GCP LB) with a public IP. 4. **ExternalName**: Maps service to an external DNS CNAME.\n\n---\n\n## 5.2 Service YAML & Useful Commands\n\n# 5.2 Service YAML & Useful Commands\n\n#\n\n## 5.2 Service YAML & Useful Commands\n### Sample Service YAML (`service.yaml`)\n```yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: nginx-service\nspec:\n  type: NodePort\n  selector:\n    app: web\n  ports:\n    - protocol: TCP\n      port: 80\n      targetPort: 80\n      nodePort: 30080\n```\n---\n### Service Commands\n```bash\n# Create Service\nkubectl apply -f service.yaml\n\n# List all Services\nkubectl get services\n\n# Inspect Service Endpoints\nkubectl get endpoints nginx-service\n\n# Delete Service\nkubectl delete service nginx-service\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5.3 Roles & RoleBindings\n\n# 5.3 Roles & RoleBindings\n\n## Roles & Bindings\nConfigure Role and ClusterRoles verbs permissions and map them.\n\n---\n\n## 5.4 Security Context & Pod Security\n\n# 5.4 Security Context & Pod Security\n\n## Security Contexts\nRun container processes as non-root users and set root limits.\n\n---\n\n## 5.5 Node Scheduling\n\n# 5.5 Node Scheduling\n\n## Node Scheduling\nControl workload node assignment scopes using selectors.\n\n---\n\n## 5.6 Taints, Tolerations & Affinity\n\n# 5.6 Taints, Tolerations & Affinity\n\n## Advanced Scheduling\nConfigure node taints, tolerations, and affinity rules.\n\n---\n\n## 5.7 Troubleshooting Kubernetes\n\n# 5.7 Troubleshooting Kubernetes\n\n## Troubleshooting\nDiagnose CrashLoopBackOff, ImagePullBackOff, and Pending states.\n\n---\n\n## 5.8 Practice: Secure & Troubleshoot a Cluster\n\n# 5.8 Practice: Secure & Troubleshoot a Cluster\n\n## ⚠️ Practice Only\nConfigure ServiceAccounts, RBAC roles, and troubleshoot failed Pod configurations.",
